117:   maker of a website, with help on invented pages (g2-who-made-it); a list of sources with title and author, and
118:   crediting sources by author and title (g2-credit-line, owned); seeing when information answers the research
119:   question and organizing it into categories with a teacher's tool (g2-fact-sort); not all information is true, and
120:   drawing a conclusion with guidance (g2-two-books-differ); a product explaining main ideas, a first sense of
121:   audience, presenting in more than one way and comparing new ideas with what was known (g2-research-share); shared
122:   research, and acknowledging others' ideas and asking others (g2-group-research). Met without a row change: one's
123:   own strengths and a goal, and "what do I wonder about now?" (the self-check, The inquiry arc); revising from the
124:   teacher's feedback (the respond days); following a modeled inquiry process each session (the cycle run each unit).
125:   Differences, each needing a row note (Row changes in For the lead, item 1): "I wonder" questions made
126:   independently, a bold skill (each child first writes their own, g2-question-to-research); periodicals and globes,
127:   and designated online encyclopedias and databases (a children's magazine and a globe join the kinds; a page the
128:   teacher chose stands in for the online ones, since no device or database is assumed, g2-kinds-of-sources); the
129:   bold skills on library rules and returning resources on time, and on the school's rules for computer use (kept in
130:   the shelf and device routine, g2-catalog-lookup); the bold skill on notes as words, phrases and drawings, not
131:   copied sentences (g2-fact-sort; key-word notes planned by the student stay in grade 3). Left out: main ideas and
132:   key details, story points of view, predictions, opinions with evidence, folktales and multicultural texts, text
133:   features as reading (index and glossary), and media against print (ELA grade 2: e2-main-topic-paragraphs,
134:   e2-points-of-view, e2-opinion, e2-fables-folktales, e2-text-features; STANDARD.md section 4; C12's voices record
135:   covers who appears in the source sets); one or two key words and the website against the database (grade 3,
136:   g3-key-words, one grade on; no database assumed); cyberbullying (computer science grade 2, g2-online-consequences,
137:   and health grade 3, g3-v-bullying); technology tools for products (no device is assumed); design thinking and the
138:   social and emotional cells (science, computer science and SEL). No row is two or more grades from its cell.
