206: | 1, mid-year | 2 | 1 | 1 | Week 13, one session, about 14 minutes for 30, all sheet and pointing items so the whole class answers at once. It samples unit 1 on new cases: three new questions, each matched to a source-kind picture with a short "because" (g2-kinds-of-sources, about 8 minutes); one question-word question a book could answer about a new picture (g2-question-to-research, about 4 minutes); and a scanned pointing item, the question a book could answer against one nobody can look up (about 2 minutes). Unit 2, which ended the week before, is not re-tested: its end-of-unit result is reused unscored, as a class count of the children who met each move, written on this check's sheet before unit 2's checklist is thrown away, so no per-child record outlives its unit (APPROACH.md, K to 2). The respond day (week 14) reteaches the missed step in small groups from the check's sheet, ending with one fresh try |
