data/plans/later.csv:30:L29,done,2026-11-15,Cory,ELA grade 10: Frankenstein source edition (Project Gutenberg 41445),Before ELA grade 10 days are written,"ELA grade 10 fix report asks data/library/sources.csv to point shelley-frank at Project Gutenberg 41445 (the 1818 text) instead of 84. 41445 is not in library/_sources yet, so the change needs a download first; a download needs Cory's yes (structure-pass-ela-2026-11-15.md, Skipped). Done 2026-11-15 (Cory said go ahead): fetched pg 41445 into library/_sources/gutenberg/41445, sources.csv points at it, library/frankenstein/text.md reprocessed as the 1818 text in three volumes with Walton's letters (library_process.py FIRST_AT and FIXES); library_check unchanged."
data/plans/later.csv:31:L30,done,2026-11-15,Cory,ELA grade 12: second audience at home and the paired history audience,Before ELA grade 12 unit plans,"ELA grade 12 fix report, For Cory: in a one-child, one-parent home there is no second listener, so the contrasting-audience performance cannot be finished there; and ELA's internal panels do not give the paired history course its audience beyond the classroom. An audience call (Cory). Lead recommendation 2026-11-15: one spine, two routes. The contrast is defined by the audience relationship and expertise, not by headcount. Classroom: student panels with the teacher as lead judge; the second audience is another class, staff, or the history capstone's outside venue (also meets D4.3.9-12, audiences outside the classroom). Home: the parent is the live first audience and lead judge; the second audience is a real listener outside the home, chosen from a menu (a relative or family friend live by phone or video; a library, co-op or community group; or a public written venue such as a letter to a local official or a public comment). Fallback: two contrasting forms to two outside audiences, the parent giving live questions. Quality held equal by the same rubric rows, a planning sheet showing what changed between audiences (the SL.11-12.6 evidence), and a short reflection. Safety: student-chosen and parent-approved; Curio Class collects and posts nothing. One shared outside audience serves ELA 12 unit 8 and US History II unit 12. Approved by Cory 2026-11-15: apply in ELA grade 12 unit 8 and US History II unit 12 plans."
data/plans/later.csv:33:L32,open,2026-11-15,Lead,ELA text record: edition and rights for every text,With each ELA unit plan batch (Cory 2026-11-15: fill as we go),"data/plans/ela-texts.csv edition, rights_basis and rights_checked are empty for most rows (skeleton spot check 2026-11-15). plan-codex-ela.md now asks each unit writer to give the edition and rights basis of every text in field 10; the lead copies them into ela-texts.csv after each batch, checking library/ and data/library/sources.csv for public-domain texts. Close when every anchor row has all three."
data/plans/later.csv:44:L43,done,2026-11-15,Cory,"Say what ""smaller"" means for SEL and library courses (fewer days or fewer units)",Before the SEL and library scopes,"Left undefined by Cory's answers of 2026-11-11 (old HANDOFF); split from L13 2026-11-15. Recommendation (lead, 2026-11-15, quality and fairness first): ""smaller"" means fewer minutes a week, not fewer units. Each SEL and library course runs the whole year at one or two sessions a week (the frame states which), so every standard in its framework is still taught, practised spaced out over the year and checked; cutting units would cut standards, and these skills grow through spaced practice. It also fits how schools staff these subjects (a librarian or counselor seeing a class once a week), so a school with less staff gets the whole course, not a thinner one. Done 2026-11-15: Cory took the recommendation (""L43 and L44 can go with your recommendation""); ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md updated in place."
data/plans/later.csv:95:L94,done,2026-11-21,Agent,scripts/progression.py codes() splits ids at the first space,"At the L87 retool, before the first SEL, career or library progression check","codes() takes the first whitespace token, so all CTE ids collapse to CTE.Career and 24 SEL sub-skill names to three codes. Fix: split on the tab only, as standards.py does; then rerun every subject gate to confirm nothing else moves (docs/reviews/sel-ownership-check-2026-11-21.md). Done 2026-11-21: codes() splits on the tab only; every existing subject gate gives the same result before and after."
